&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Governance, Risk and Compliance Director to lead this team through its next phase of growth. You&#39;ll own Figma&#39;s security compliance, risk management, and governance strategy end to end - setting direction for our certification portfolio, building the risk and controls frameworks that scale with our growing business and product suite, and representing GRC to executives, the board, customers, and regulators. This is a hands-on leadership role where you&#39;ll manage and grow a team of GRC professionals while staying close to the programs, infrastructure, audits, and cross-functional relationships needed to both protect and enable the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re a strategist and team builder who is excited to scale Figma&#39;s GRC program in a rapidly evolving environment, we&#39;d love to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full time role that can be held from one of our US hubs or remotely in the United States.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do at Figma:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the strategy and roadmap for Figma&#39;s GRC program, aligning compliance, risk, and governance priorities with company objectives and the Security leadership team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Figma&#39;s certification and compliance portfolio, including SOC 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP, SOX ITGC, and GDPR, and expand coverage as Figma enters new markets and customer segments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and grow a team of compliance, risk, and governance professionals, setting priorities, developing talent, and building a culture of rigor and pragmatism&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and evolve enterprise risk and controls frameworks — including AI Governance, Risk and Compliance initiatives and control effectiveness monitoring — that scale across technical and business stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage relationships with external auditors, assessors, and regulators, and oversee audit cycles from planning through remediation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct the selection and optimization of GRC platforms and tooling, and maintain the lifecycle of security policies, standards, and procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales, Legal, and Customer Trust on security questionnaires, customer audits, contracts, and trust-related communications that support the sales lifecycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scale enterprise risk reporting and report on program health, risk posture, and audit readiness to executive and board-level audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&#39;d love to hear from you if you have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in information security, compliance, or risk management, including at least 4 years leading or managing a GRC, security, or compliance team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep, hands-on experience with frameworks such as SOC 2 and ISO 27001, including leading programs through multiple audit cycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of building GRC programs from the ground up or scaling them through high-growth stages, ideally at a SaaS or platform company, including experience operating in a public company environment with SOX ITGC requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive presence and exceptional written and verbal communication skills, with demonstrated ability to build cross-functional partnerships across Security, Legal, IT, Sales, and Engineering and translate technical risk into business terms for executives, the board, and customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing compliance programs for emerging products, including AI-enabled products, with a strong understanding of cloud-based technologies and their GRC implications, and a builder&#39;s mindset comfortable with ambiguity as the program scales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;While it&#39;s not required, it&#39;s an added plus if you also have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supported FedRAMP authorization, SSP development, 3PAO coordination, or continuous monitoring activities&lt;/li&gt;
