&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an Immigration Program Manager to support Figma&#39;s growing Immigration and Global Mobility programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role you will serve as a primary point of contact for visa-sponsored Figmates, managing immigration cases and compliance while providing a high-touch employee experience. You&#39;ll also support international relocations and broader global mobility programs and get exposure to M&amp;amp;A and international expansion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll partner closely with immigration counsel and teams across People, Finance, Legal, Talent Acquisition, and Payroll to improve our processes, resources, reporting, budgeting, vendor management, and program administration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full time role that can be held from one of our US hubs or remotely in the United States.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do at Figma:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as primary contact for Figmates and stakeholders on immigration inquiries, visa assessments, case status, and strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a high-volume immigration case portfolio - including permanent residence processes (PERM, I-140, AOS, ILR) — across US, EMEA, JAPAC, and LATAM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with outside immigration counsel on case petition preparation, timelines, RFE responses, audits, and compliance matters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and proactively manage work authorization expirations across the foreign national population, ensuring timely renewals and escalations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with People Partners and Talent Acquisition to assess immigration sponsorship feasibility for new hires and internal transfers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain Figmate-facing immigration resources, FAQs, playbooks, and compliance documentation (PAF, etc.), and design training for key stakeholders and Figmates globally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor regulatory changes and manage internal reporting, trackers, dashboards, and I-9 compliance efforts, serving as internal POC for I-9 escalations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate international relocations and participate in global mobility, People M&amp;amp;A, and international expansion initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&#39;d love to hear from you if you have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience managing immigration for EMEA, APAC, and AMER at a global technology company or employment-based immigration law firm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep subject-matter expertise in U.S. nonimmigrant and immigrant visa categories (H-1B CAP &amp;amp; cap-exempt, L-1, O-1, TN, OPT, PERM, EB-1/EB-2, AOS, EADs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing multiple vendors and supporting complex immigration matters, including international relocations and/or assignments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with People Ops-related compliance projects, with interest in contributing beyond the immigration and global mobility functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional project management, organizational, and prioritization skills, with the ability to translate complex legal concepts into crisp written and verbal communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;While it&#39;s not required, it&#39;s an added plus if you also have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting immigration needs related to M&amp;amp;A activity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong expertise in Singapore immigration and the COMPASS framework&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of international assignment management, including assignment design, cost projections, tax equalization, and assignee lifecycle support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with cross-border tax concepts - including hypo tax, shadow payroll, and equity income sourcing for mobile employees and expatriates — and equity income sourcing mechanics for RSUs and stock options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing business traveler compliance programs, including short-term assignment tracking and permanent establishment risk identification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
